---
title: Registry
description: How components are cataloged, and how to install them elsewhere.
order: 2
---

Every component, block, and utility lives under `registry/items/<section>/<name>/`, with three files:

- `_registry.svx` — frontmatter metadata plus a prose usage guide.
- `_preview.svelte` — the live demo rendered on this site and reused as the "Code" tab's source.
- `stories/<name>.stories.svelte` — a Storybook story for the same component.

The catalog is built at request time with Vite's `import.meta.glob`, so adding a new item is just adding a new folder — no manifest to hand-maintain.

## CLI distribution

Every item is also installable into other projects via the shadcn-svelte CLI, the same way `shadcn-svelte add <name>` installs from the official registry:

```bash
bun x shadcn-svelte@latest add https://design-system-starter-svelte-docs.vercel.app/r/<name>.json
```

The "Install → CLI" tab on each item page has the exact command pre-filled. Behind the scenes, `bun run registry:build` reads every item's `_registry.svx` frontmatter, generates a `registry.json`, and runs it through `shadcn-svelte registry build` to produce the served `/r/<name>.json` files — no hand-written server endpoints. The whole registry is also available as one file at `/registry.json`.
